'''Meta Platforms, Inc.''' is an American multinational technology company headquartered in [[Menlo Park, California]]. Meta owns and operates several prominent [[social media]] platforms and communication services, including [[Facebook]], [[Instagram]], [[WhatsApp]], [[Messenger (Meta)|Messenger]] and [[Threads (social network)|Threads]]. The company also operates an [[advertising network]] for its own sites and third parties; {{As of|2023|lc=y}}, advertising accounted for 97.8 percent of its total revenue.<ref>{{cite web |date=February 1, 2024 |title=Meta Reports Fourth Quarter and Full Year 2023 Results; Initiates Quarterly Dividend |url=https://investor.fb.com/investor-news/press-release-details/2024/Meta-Reports-Fourth-Quarter-and-Full-Year-2023-Results-Initiates-Quarterly-Dividend/default.aspx |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240202004957/https://investor.fb.com/investor-news/press-release-details/2024/Meta-Reports-Fourth-Quarter-and-Full-Year-2023-Results-Initiates-Quarterly-Dividend/default.aspx |archive-date=February 2, 2024 |access-date=February 2, 2024 |website=Facebook Investor Relations}}</ref> Meta is considered part of the [[Big Tech]] group, alongside [[Nvidia]], [[Microsoft]], [[Apple Inc.|Apple]], [[Alphabet Inc.|Alphabet]], and [[Amazon (company)|Amazon]].

The company was originally established in 2004 as '''TheFacebook, Inc.''',<ref>{{cite magazine |title=Facebook's Very First SEC Filing |first=Alexis C. |last=Madrigal |magazine=[[The Atlantic]] |date=January 31, 2012 |url=https://www.theatlantic.com/technology/archive/2012/01/facebooks-very-first-sec-filing/252282/ |access-date=November 3, 2021 |archive-date=November 17, 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211117130121/https://www.theatlantic.com/technology/archive/2012/01/facebooks-very-first-sec-filing/252282/ |url-status=live }}</ref> and was renamed '''Facebook, Inc.''' in 2005.<ref>{{cite web |date=September 1, 2020 |title=Facebook Inc. Certificate of Incorporation |url=https://s21.q4cdn.com/399680738/files/doc_downloads/governance_documents/FB_CertificateOfIncorporation.pdf |access-date=October 28, 2021 |archive-date=September 23, 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210923202624/https://s21.q4cdn.com/399680738/files/doc_downloads/governance_documents/FB_CertificateOfIncorporation.pdf |url-status=live }}</ref> In 2021, it rebranded as Meta Platforms, Inc. to reflect a strategic shift toward developing the [[metaverse]]—an interconnected digital ecosystem spanning [[virtual reality|virtual]] and [[augmented reality]] technologies.<ref name="theverge20211019"/><ref name="meta-blog"/><ref>{{cite news |last=Dwoskin |first=Elizabeth |date=October 28, 2021 |title=Facebook is changing its name to Meta as it focuses on the virtual world |url=https://www.washingtonpost.com/technology/2021/10/28/facebook-meta-name-change/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211028182314/https://www.washingtonpost.com/technology/2021/10/28/facebook-meta-name-change/ |archive-date=October 28, 2021 |access-date=October 28, 2021 |newspaper=[[The Washington Post]]}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |date=October 28, 2021 |title=Facebook announces name change to Meta in rebranding effort |url=https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2021/oct/28/facebook-name-change-rebrand-meta |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211028183343/https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2021/oct/28/facebook-name-change-rebrand-meta |archive-date=October 28, 2021 |access-date=October 29, 2021 |website=[[The Guardian]]}}</ref>

In 2023, Meta was ranked 31st on the ''[[Forbes Global 2000|Forbes]]'' [[Forbes Global 2000|Global 2000]] list of the world's largest public companies.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.forbes.com/lists/global2000/?sh=51d599675ac0|title=The Global 2000 2023|website=[[Forbes]]|access-date=2024-02-07|archive-date=2024-01-29|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240129031905/https://www.forbes.com/lists/global2000/?sh=4f5ab07e5ac0}}</ref> As of 2022, it was the world's third-largest spender on [[research and development]], with R&D expenses totaling US$35.3 billion.<ref>{{cite web |last=Irwin-Hunt |first=Alex |title=Top 100 global innovation leaders |url=https://www.fdiintelligence.com/content/feature/global-innovation-leaders-2022-edition-82527 |access-date=2024-06-16 |website=[[fDi Intelligence]] |date=June 19, 2023}}</ref>

